{"slug": "different-types-of-communication-protocols", "question": "What Are the Different Types of Communication Protocols?", "body_html": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Communication protocols are of two types: inter system protocols, which link separate devices such as a computer and a microcontroller, and intra system protocols, which link chips on the same circuit board.</p><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:8px 0 4px;font-size:16px;\"><tr style=\"background:#1a2b4a;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Protocol</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Type</th><th style=\"padding:8px;text-align:left;\">Signal Lines</th></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">UART</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Inter system</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Tx, Rx</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">USART</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Inter system</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Tx, Rx plus clock</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">USB</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Inter system</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">D+, D−</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">I2C</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Intra system</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">SDA, SCL</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#eef4fb\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">SPI</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Intra system</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">MOSI, MISO, SCLK, SS</td></tr><tr style=\"background:#fff\"><td style=\"padding:8px;\">CAN</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">Intra system</td><td style=\"padding:8px;\">CAN High, CAN Low</td></tr></table>"}